@format 1
@id section-creation.add-at-cursor
@title Add at cursor
@section Section creation
@area In Split tab
@entry add-dispatch
@summary Create one new unnamed section from the current cursor forward, covering only creation and excluding later editing, deletion, naming, and renaming.
@related section-creation.common.compass-buttons, section-creation.common.keyboard-shortcuts, section-creation.common.forward-section-plan, section-creation.common.apply-created-state
@tag section
@tag split
@tag creation
@tag add

@alias flow = Cadroue.UIShell.PFlow.PFlow
@alias segment = Cadroue.Application.LSegment

[add-dispatch] addSection dispatch request <input>
~ This starts with addSection dispatch request.
[Technical explanation]
= The request came from the Split Compass Add button or the currently bound SectionAdd shortcut.
> dispatch-guard

[dispatch-guard] Active Split flow guard <decision>
~ The program checks active Split flow guard.
[Technical explanation]
- PFlowShortcutDispatch rejects commands unless this flow is command-active with a loaded spool, and the addSection case additionally requires section UI to be active @ flow.PFlowShortcutDispatch(...) / addSection
? "Rejected" > dispatch-rejected
? "Accepted" > add-handler

[dispatch-rejected] Add command ignored <output>
~ This path ends with add command ignored.
[Technical explanation]
= No section creation method is called.

[add-handler] Prepare Add creation <decision>
~ The program checks prepare Add creation.
[Technical explanation]
- PFlowSectionAdd requires section editing to be enabled plus a spool and nonblank source path; on acceptance it resets pFlowSegmentFired and chooses the color as current section count modulo the active palette count @ flow.PFlowSectionAdd(...)
@ flow.PFlowColorRead(...)
? "Editing disabled or media/source unavailable" > add-rejected
? "Creation request accepted" > segment-add

[add-rejected] Add creation blocked <output>
~ This path ends with add creation blocked.
[Technical explanation]
= No section state changes.

[segment-add] Ask LSegment to add at the cursor <process>
~ This step handles ask section-planning step to add at the cursor.
[Technical explanation]
- Pass cursor, media duration, computed color, and the current overlap policy to LSegmentAdd, which asks LPieceAdd for the actual creation plan @ segment.LSegmentAdd(...)
@ property flow.PFlowOverlapAllowed
> map:section-creation.common.forward-section-plan
